I take my first look at the Great Barrier Reef on my first liveaboard dive trip. I am at Milln Reef, a reef located 55 kilometres off the coast of Cairns. So grateful of the visibility, dive conditions and the ability to be able to dive in one of the seven wonders of the world. These are my top clips of the day. Some epic sightings and encounters with turtles, butterflyfish, rabbitfish and more.

## Dive stats

- **Location:** Milln Reef, QLD
- **Date:** 20 June 2026
- **Depth:** Max Depth 19.4m, Average Depth 11.2m
- **Visibility:** 15-25m

## Highlights

Hawksbill Turtle, Green Turtle, Moorish Idol, Maori Wrasse
